 - **Restricted Domain:** When convolving over a restricted domain $X$, the contribution of the original distribution is clamped to black by $X$ [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per convolution, dominated by LUT lookups and interpolation. This is significantly faster than Monte Carlo integration [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing two LUTs: $50^3 \times 2$ floats for SGGX-GGX and $20^3 \times 2$ floats for SGGX-SG. This is a small, fixed memory overhead [S1, unofficial].
