 ## Background
-This technique is part of the ABSDF (Aggregated Bidirectional Scattering Distribution Function) framework for efficient scene appearance aggregation. It was introduced by Yang Zhou, Tao Huang, Ravi Ramamoorthi, Pradeep Sen, and Ling-Qi Yan in their 2010 paper "Efficient Scene Appearance Aggregation for Level-of-Detail Rendering" presented at the Symposium on Interactive 3D Graphics (SI3D) [S1, unofficial]. The method leverages the properties of SGGX distributions and precomputed fits to accelerate the convolution of microflake distributions with other microfacet or spherical distributions [S1, unofficial].
